---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import PageIntro from '../../components/PageIntro.astro';
import { site } from '../../lib/config';
---
<Layout lang="en" title="Getting started with Stille" description="Install Stille for Android, exchange profile or one-time invites, and troubleshoot peer-to-peer connections." canonical="/en/guide/">
<Header />
<main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="document-page wrap">
  <PageIntro label="Getting started" title="Your first conversation" description="Install Stille on both devices. Choose a name and exchange an invite — no phone number required." />
  <div class="guide-intro"><div class="prose"><h2>First launch</h2><p>Download the APK, install it, then choose your language, name and theme. Contacts can see your name; you can change it in your profile.</p><a class="text-link" href="/en/download/">Download and install →</a></div><img src="/assets/owl-invite.svg" width="190" height="177" alt="Owl holding an invitation" /></div>
  <section class="guide-section" aria-labelledby="invites-heading"><div class="section-heading"><h2 id="invites-heading">Invites</h2><p>Don't post active invite codes publicly.<br/>Share them only with the intended person.</p></div><div class="guide-columns"><div class="prose"><h3>To invite someone</h3><ol class="instructions"><li>Open Add contact in Chats or Contacts.</li><li>Create a one-time invite or share your permanent profile link. Only share a permanent link with people you want to add.</li><li>Send its link or show the QR code in person.</li></ol></div><div class="prose"><h3>To accept an invite</h3><ol class="instructions"><li>Open the full invite link on Android. If prompted, choose Stille.</li><li>Profile links use <code>/invite/i/</code> or <code>/invite/i3/</code>; the app handles the code locally.</li><li>If the app does not open, scan the HTTPS QR with Stille's built-in scanner.</li></ol></div></div><p class="notice">The site does not store or resolve profile codes. Availability of Android App Links depends on the installed app version and domain verification.</p></section>
  <section class="document-grid guide-section" aria-labelledby="connection-heading"><div><h2 id="connection-heading">Connection troubleshooting</h2><p class="section-description">Peer-to-peer messaging needs a route between devices.</p></div><div class="prose"><h3>Devices nearby</h3><p>Invites without an address are designed to connect over the same local network. Some routers and guest Wi-Fi networks block device discovery.</p><h3>Devices on different networks</h3><p>Internet access alone is not enough. A reachable network address or a configured relay may be needed. If the contact does not appear, check the connection and ask the other person to review their network settings.</p><h3>Invite not accepted</h3><p>Check that the full link or code was copied. The app checks the invite when you add it. If it is invalid, ask the sender to create another.</p><a href={site.android} rel="noreferrer">Android client documentation ↗</a></div></section>
  <section class="faq-section" aria-labelledby="faq-heading"><div><h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently asked questions</h2></div><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>Does the link open the app automatically?</summary><p>The app can handle <code>stille://</code> and <code>https://stille.im/invite/</code> links. Automatic opening of HTTPS links depends on Android and domain verification, which is not configured yet. If Stille does not open, paste the invite into Add contact or scan its QR code in the app.</p></details><details><summary>Does Stille need my phone number?</summary><p>No. Choose a name for your profile and connect through an invite.</p></details><details><summary>Does this site connect devices?</summary><p>No. The website only presents invite links; Stille handles the connection between devices.</p></details><details><summary>Where can I report a problem?</summary><p>Open an <a href={`${site.android}/issues`}>issue on GitHub</a>. Include your app version and steps to reproduce, but never share active invite codes or private messages.</p></details></div></section>
</main><Footer />
</Layout>
